> Check captured BN moments before any moving update

For two one-channel values(1,3), the batch mean is 2, population variance 1 and
unbiased variance 2. Normalized values are ±1/sqrt(1+epsilon). Conditional affine
scales(2,3) and shifts(-.5,.25) then act separately per row. The source uses
population variance for normalization and source-rounded unbiased variance for
moving state. With old mean 0/variance 1 and Float32-rounded retention.9, the next
mean is about.200000048 and variance 1.100000024. Using population variance in
the moving update would incorrectly keep variance 1.

`capture_batch_norm` returns normalized values and live moment captures without
writing existing statistics. `batch_norm_moving_values` computes detached candidates.
This split lets the fitting loop write G first and then commit the moments captured
before that write, without recomputing them at updated weights. The source divides
by sqrt(var+double(1e-5f)); a fused BN affine path has different Float32 rounding.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/big_gan_bn.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n         = dm::nn;
  auto              t = n::DType::Float64;
  n::ParameterStore stats(0, t);
  auto              x       = n::tensor({1., 3.}, {2, 1}, t);
  auto              capture = n::capture_batch_norm(stats, "bn", x, true);
  auto              conditional =
      capture.value * n::tensor({2., 3.}, {2, 1}, t) + n::tensor({-.5, .25}, {2, 1}, t);
  auto next = n::batch_norm_moving_values(
      stats.at("bn/moving_mean"),
      stats.at("bn/moving_var"),
      capture.mean,
      capture.unbiased_variance);
  if (capture.mean.at({0}) != 2 || capture.unbiased_variance.at({0}) != 2 ||
      stats.at("bn/moving_mean").at({0}) != 0)
    throw std::runtime_error("capture toy");
  std::print(
      "Captured mean={}, unbiased variance={}; candidate saved mean={}, variance={}. Existing "
      "state stays0/1.\n",
      capture.mean.at({0}),
      capture.unbiased_variance.at({0}),
      next.mean.at({0}),
      next.variance.at({0}));
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-3.5, 6.)
      .lines({1., 2.}, capture.value.to_vector<double>(), "Unparameterized BN", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .points({1., 2.}, capture.value.to_vector<double>(), "", {37, 99, 235}, 4.)
      .lines(
          {1., 2.},
          conditional.to_vector<double>(),
          "Per-row conditional affine",
          {220, 38, 38},
          2.)
      .points({1., 2.}, conditional.to_vector<double>(), "", {220, 38, 38}, 4.)
      .x_label("Observation; batch values are1 and3")
      .y_label("Normalized or conditionally affine value")
      .title("Capture moments first; write moving state explicitly later")
      .save_svg("build/big_gan_bn.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Captured mean=2, unbiased variance=2; candidate saved mean=0.20000004768371582, variance=1.100000023841858. Existing state stays0/1.
\image(figures/big_gan_bn.svg)
