\caption(The conditional scale and shift in this hand example are supplied constants. The trained model obtains them from separate spectral dense maps of class embedding and latent chunk.)
\alttext(Two normalized values and their separately scaled/shifted conditional outputs; printed moments distinguish population normalization from unbiased moving variance.)

> Check a class projection without changing the image features

A projection discriminator adds a class-feature inner product to a source score.
For fixed features phi=(1,2,3,.5), source score.25 and two supplied effective class
embeddings e 0=(1,0,0,0), e 1=(0,1,0,0), the projection terms are 1 and 2, so total
scores are 1.25 and 2.25. Changing only the class leaves phi and the source term
unchanged. These supplied features/embeddings isolate the algebra; they are separate
from the learned checkpoint. The trained source uses ten requested classes and a
spectrally normalized 10x 4 projection table.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/big_gan_projection_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  auto t          = n::DType::Float64;
  auto classes    = n::tensor({0, 1}, {2}, n::DType::Int64),
       onehot     = n::cast(n::one_hot(classes, 2), t);
  auto table      = n::tensor({1., 0., 0., 0., 0., 1., 0., 0.}, {2, 4}, t),
       features   = n::tile(n::tensor({1., 2., 3., .5}, {1, 4}, t), {2, 1});
  auto projection = n::sum(features * n::matmul(onehot, table), {1}, true),
       source = n::full({2, 1}, .25, t), score = source + projection;
  if (score.at({0, 0}) != 1.25 || score.at({1, 0}) != 2.25)
    throw std::runtime_error("projection toy");
  std::print(
      "Fixed features/source; class0 score={}, class1 score={}.\n",
      score.at({0, 0}),
      score.at({1, 0}));
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(0., 4.)
      .points({1., 2.}, source.to_vector<double>(), "Source term", {120, 120, 120}, 5.)
      .points({1., 2.}, projection.to_vector<double>(), "Class projection", {37, 99, 235}, 5.)
      .points({1., 2.}, score.to_vector<double>(), "Total raw score", {220, 38, 38}, 5.)
      .x_label("Class condition: class0 at1; class1 at2")
      .y_label("Raw score component")
      .title("Class changes the projection term, without a class posterior")
      .save_svg("build/big_gan_projection_toy.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Fixed features/source; class0 score=1.25, class1 score=2.25.
\image(figures/big_gan_projection_toy.svg)
// result_end
