> Held-out inference images and the source evaluation convention

| Fixed final diagnostic | Value |
|---|---:|
| D hinge objective, batch-statistics fake |1.0547924042|
| G source term, batch-statistics fake |-0.0504588634|
| G modified raw-kernel penalty |1.4359538625e-7|
| G total objective |-0.0504587181|
| Maximum class change in generated pixels |0.1876689494|
| Maximum class change in real-image projection score |0.4659057856|
| Frozen-statistics single/batch inference maximum error |0|

The gallery keeps the first 40 fixed test codes and their supplied classes, without
choosing attractive outputs. These are saved-statistics inference images, whereas the
reported game losses above use batch-statistics fake images from the same 200-row test
bank. A negative generator source term is a raw-score objective value, not a negative
image error or a realism metric. No requested-class recognition accuracy, IS, FID,
seed sweep or paper-scale result is claimed by this short run.

