> Compare the two saved generator paths on the same codes

The top row uses checkpoint moving statistics. The bottom row uses batch moments
computed from the complete 200-row held-out code bank, then displays its first eight
rows. It does not recompute batch moments on only the displayed eight. Both paths use
the same weights, labels and codes; neither writes state. Standalone inference agrees
bit exactly with the combined forward's inference pixels, and the first sample has
zero measured single/batch inference difference because saved moments stay fixed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/big_gan_paths.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/big_gan/outputs.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  auto images = n::concat(
      {n::slice_axis(a.at("fake_inference"), 0, 0, 8),
       n::slice_axis(a.at("fake_training"), 0, 0, 8)},
      0);
  n::save_image_grid(images, "build/big_gan_paths.png", 8, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 8);
  std::print(
      "Top: saved BN. Bottom: batch BN from all200 test codes. Both paths leave checkpoint state "
      "unchanged.\n");
}
