// result_begin: markdown
All200 projection replays exact; maximum raw-score change=0.4659057855606079.
\image(figures/big_gan_projection.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All 200 points are retained. The additional projection_terms archive exposes source, projection, features and both scores for an independent check.)
\alttext(Original-class versus next-class discriminator scores for all held-out images, with an identity reference.)

> Zero each of the three hierarchical latent chunks

The saved controls replace one four-coordinate chunk with zero, retaining every other
coordinate and class. All three replacements affect G. The gallery uses the first eight
fixed test rows: original inference, zero stem chunk z 0, zero first-conditional chunk z 1,
then zero second-conditional chunk z 2. Effects establish that each supplied chunk matters;
they do not identify disentangled factors or independently meaningful semantic controls.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/big_gan_hierarchy.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a, h;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/big_gan/outputs.npz"))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("build/big_gan/hierarchical_controls.npz"))
    h.emplace(k, v);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> rows{n::slice_axis(a.at("fake_inference"), 0, 0, 8)};
  for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c) {
    auto image = h.at("zero_chunk" + std::to_string(c) + "_fake");
    rows.push_back(n::slice_axis(image, 0, 0, 8));
    std::print(
        "Zero chunk{}: full-bank maximum pixel effect={}\n",
        c,
        n::max(n::abs(image - a.at("fake_inference"))).item());
  }
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(rows, 0), "build/big_gan_hierarchy.png", 8, 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 8);
}
```
