> Compare rejection thresholds with frozen inference state

Columns use limits infinity,2,1,.5. Every bank starts from MT seed 6907 and accepts
its own stream after thresholding, so columns are not clipped or rescaled versions
of a shared accepted vector. Each displayed row holds its requested class fixed across
columns, using source labels i%10. The full banks have 200 rows per threshold, while this
original gallery keeps the first eight rows. All normalization and learned state remain
frozen. This comparison demonstrates the supplied distribution control; it is not an
IS/FID evaluation of a quality/diversity tradeoff in this tiny model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/big_gan_truncation.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
